# Multilingual Synchronization Rules

- **Primary Source:** French (`lang="fr"`) located at the root of the project is the master language for all content, design, and structural changes.
- **Automatic 3-Language Propagation:** Whenever any edit is made to a root French page (`*.html`), the corresponding changes MUST immediately be applied to both the English (`en/*.html`) and Arabic (`ar/*.html`) versions.
- **Language Requirements:**
  - Arabic (`ar/`) pages must preserve `dir="rtl"` and accurate Arabic terminology.
  - English (`en/`) pages must use clean, professional B2B phrasing.
  - Verify relative links, language switches, and metadata across all 3 versions for strict parity.

